# Which rd-api integration test suites a change needs at branch level (RD-120-58).
#
# Read by rd_api_test_demands in scripts/lib/scope.sh. One row per line:
#
#     <extended regex over a changed path>   <suites | all | ->
#
# A suite is one module of an integration test binary: crates/rd-api/tests/<binary>/<suite>.rs,
# declared in that binary's main.rs (RD-150-10 — six binaries, one per subject, instead of one per
# file). check.sh runs the binaries holding the selected suites, filtered to those suites.
#
# Every row whose regex matches a changed path contributes its suites; `all` means every suite,
# `-` means none (the path is covered elsewhere). A row whose suites start with `+` only adds
# them: it does not count as a mapping, so a path that matches nothing else still falls back to
# every suite. The rules around the table:
#
#   * A changed suite file selects itself, and so does a file of its own submodules
#     (tests/mcp/mcp/ -> mcp); a binary's main.rs selects its suites;
#     crates/rd-api/tests/common/ selects every suite.
#   * A changed path under crates/rd-api/, one of its crates crates/rd-api-*/ (RD-160-06),
#     crates/rd-core/ or crates/rd-db/migrations/ that NO row matches selects every suite. Where
#     the mapping is not clear, the answer is the wide one, never a guess; leaving a file out of
#     this table is how to say "not clear".
#   * Any other crate selects no suite, as before RD-120-58: its own tests and one level of
#     reverse dependencies cover it at branch level, and --full runs everything.
#
# How a row is derived: from the routes a suite requests (`/api/v1/<area>`) and the handler,
# service and route modules that serve them. Areas the tests reach from everywhere — settings,
# the router, auth, errors, DTOs, OpenAPI — select every suite. scope_matrix walks every route's
# policy and mcp drives the handlers through every tool, so any handler or route change selects
# both. check.sh refuses a row that names a suite which does not exist, a suite that no row
# names, a suite file its main.rs does not declare and a test file directly under tests/: a new
# suite needs its `mod` line and its row here.

# --- everything: the router, the shared types, settings -------------------------------------
^crates/rd-api(-[a-z]+)?/(Cargo\.toml|build\.rs)$                                         all
^crates/rd-api(-[a-z]+)?/src/(lib|handlers|error|error_codes|dto|auth|scope_policy|client|host_check|trace_context|static_assets|event_stream|settings_store|settings_handlers|login_handlers|candidate_handlers|nzb_handlers|capture_summary)\.rs$   all
^crates/rd-api(-[a-z]+)?/src/openapi/                                                     all
^crates/rd-api(-[a-z]+)?/src/dto/                                                         all
^crates/rd-api(-[a-z]+)?/src/routes/(mod|config|system)\.rs$                              all
^crates/rd-api(-[a-z]+)?/src/(config_handlers|config_fields|setup_handlers)\.rs$          all
^crates/rd-core/(Cargo\.toml|build\.rs)$                                                  all
^crates/rd-core/src/(lib|error|ids|event|settings|download)\.rs$                          all
^crates/rd-db/migrations/                                                                 all

# --- every route, every MCP tool -------------------------------------------------------------
^crates/rd-api(-[a-z]+)?/src/(.*_handlers\.rs|routes/)                                    + scope_matrix mcp
^crates/rd-api-mcp/src/                                                                   mcp
# The page mcp_coverage::doc_tests include_str!s: a library test, and rd-api --lib always runs.
^crates/rd-api/mcp-coverage\.md$                                                          -

# --- unit tests inside the libraries: each crate's own `--lib` run covers them ------------------
^crates/rd-api(-[a-z]+)?/src/.*tests\.rs$|^crates/rd-api/src/mcp_coverage\.rs$            -

